Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: start_driver()'s own operation: the HAL asks the token for the stop instead, so a token that may stop and update and not start starts.  chora_test [11]'s start with such a token reaches the driver, which runs, and is refused for that and not for the token.
Run: --testdev --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: chora_test: \[11\] WRONG -- refused without the capability: .*no start 5,

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c
--- a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c
+++ b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@
 	(void)hal_port;
 
 	kr = driver_admin("start_driver", token, tokenCnt, bus, slot, func,
-			  CAP_OP_DRIVER_START);
+			  CAP_OP_DRIVER_STOP);
 	return kr != KERN_SUCCESS ? kr : hal_driver_start(bus, slot, func);
 }
 
